          "number": 2,
          "letter": "",
          "english": "The temptation for those in charge of education budgets to trade teachers for technology could be so strong that they ignore the disadvantages of distance learning. School facilities are expensive to build and maintain, and teachers are expensive to employ. Online classes do not require buildings and each class can host hundreds of people simultaneously, resulting in greater savings, thus increasing the temptation of distance education for those concerned more about budgets than learning. But moving away from a traditional classroom in which a living, breathing human being teaches and interacts with students daily would be a disaster. Physically attending school has hidden benefits: getting up every morning, interacting with peers, and building relationships with teachers are essential skills to cultivate in young people. Moreover, schools should be more than simple institutions of traditional learning. They are now places that provide meals. They are places where students receive counseling and other support.",
          "chinese": "对于那些负责教育预算的人来说,用技术取代教师的诱惑可能会如此强烈,以至于他们忽视了远程学习的弊端。学校设施的建设和维护成本高昂,而雇用教师也很昂贵。在线课程不需要建筑物,每个班级可以同时容纳数百人,从而节省更多开支,这增加了那些更关心预算而非学习的人对远程教育的诱惑。但是,抛弃传统课堂——在那里有一个活生生的人每天教学并与学生互动——将是一场灾难。实际到校上学有着隐藏的益处:每天早上起床、与同龄人互动以及与教师建立关系,这些都是年轻人需要培养的基本技能。此外,学校应该不仅仅是传统学习的简单机构。它们现在是提供餐食的地方,是学生接受咨询和其他支持的地方。",
